  "body": "## What changed\n\n`scripts/package-linux.sh`: the RPM spec's `%files` list now names the hicolor icons. It gains one glob line:\n\n```\n/usr/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps/camcraft.png\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nCommit 55c8bcc6 installs the logo in seven sizes (16 to 512) under `/usr/share/icons/hicolor/<size>/apps/`. The `%files` list did not name them. Thus `rpmbuild` stopped with \"Installed (but unpackaged) file(s) found\", and the v0.20.0 release run 43644441134 made no Linux packages (job `linux`, step \"Assemble Linux packages\").\n\n## Tests\n\n- `bash -n scripts/package-linux.sh`: no syntax error.\n- RPM `%files` lines accept glob patterns. The pattern matches the seven installed paths in the error log of the run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine on our side has `rpmbuild`, so the rpm was not built locally. A run of `release.yml`, or of `scripts/package-linux.sh` on a host with rpmbuild, proves the fix.\n- The deb, AppImage and tar.gz parts of the script do not change.\n\nThis PR changes `scripts/`. A reviewer reads it and does not build it (AGENTS.md), and it waits for the maintainer.\n\nChangelog: The Linux release packages build again: the RPM now lists the application icons (#1719)\n\nFixes #1719\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
